{
  "sourceLanguage" : "en",
  "strings" : {
    "How to turn on file transfer" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "%@, %@" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@, %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Restart" : {

    },
    "%@ · %@" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ · %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "**Use It** connects the address and remembers it for that device. **Ignore** leaves it unused until Ferry restarts." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Anyone on a network can claim a device's serial number. So when a new address answers as a device Ferry already knows, Ferry does not use it on its own: the menu asks “Is *address* your *device*?”" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Is this address your device?" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "**Forget** disconnects the device and forgets its addresses. Ferry no longer connects to it by itself." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry remembers each device it connects this way by its serial number, and connects to it again when Ferry starts and when adb restarts. A remembered device it cannot reach shows **Not connected**, with **Connect** to try again." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Remembered devices" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Click **Connect by Address…**, type the device's IP address or name, and click **Connect**. Ferry uses adb's usual port unless you add another after a colon. If the device asks, tap **Allow** on it: the menu shows that it is waiting until you do." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry then connects to the address the device offers for connections, which is not the one it paired on." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "On the device, open **Developer options** → **Wireless debugging** and choose **Pair device with pairing code**. In Ferry's menu, click **Pair with Code…**, enter the IP address and port and the code the device shows, and click **Pair**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turning it on restarts ADB on the device, so Ferry refuses while the device has a transfer, a screen recording or a log running: let it finish, then try again." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "With the device on USB debugging and connected by cable, click **Use over Wi-Fi** under its name. Ferry reads the device's Ethernet and Wi-Fi addresses, turns on ADB over the network if it is off, and connects to the first address that answers. Connect the device to Ethernet or Wi-Fi first." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Use over Wi-Fi suits a device already on USB debugging, such as a NetAlly tester or a phone with Android 8 to 10. Pair with Code is for Android 11 and newer. Connect by Address is for a device that already accepts ADB over the network." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry can reach a device over ADB on your network as well as by cable. It never searches the network: it connects only to addresses you give it, and to the addresses a device on USB debugging reports for itself. A device that is also on a cable is always served by the cable." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Connect over the network" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry is using this device. Wait for its transfers, screen recording and log to finish, then try again." : {

    },
    "%@ used, %@ free" : {

    },
    "%@ · %@ free" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ · %2$@ free"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ferry can't watch USB for devices, so it looks for them every 30 seconds." : {

    },
    "A notification says when the files are on the device or the app is installed, or why not." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Control-click files on the Mac and choose **Send to** and the device. Ferry copies them into the Download folder on the device's internal storage. Ferry's button in the Finder toolbar has the same menu once you add it with **View** → **Customize Toolbar**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Folders, packages and links can't be sent from this menu. Copy a folder into the device's location in Finder instead, and compress a package into a .zip first." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "If Download already has a file with the same name, Ferry keeps it and saves yours beside it as **name (conflict from Mac)**. Sending never replaces a file." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Lines shown: %lld of %lld" : {

    },
    "%lld%%" : {

    },
    "%lld%%, charging" : {

    },
    "%lld%%, discharging" : {

    },
    "%lld%%, full" : {

    },
    "%lld%%, not charging" : {

    },
    "%lld." : {

    },
    "A device Ferry reaches over ADB (USB · ADB or Wi-Fi · ADB in the menu) shows Install App…, Screenshot and Record Screen under its name, and a Developer Tools menu. A device on file transfer shows More Tools with USB Debugging… instead." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A device on your network is waiting for you to allow this Mac. Tap **Allow** on the device." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ferry turns the device's screen on before a screenshot or a recording, so a screen that was off is not captured black. A recording of a screen that does not change has a single frame." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A file changed on both sides" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A file the device changed since Finder last showed it is not deleted. Finder puts it back with the device's version." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A folder is deleted with its contents only if Finder has shown everything in it, at every level, as it is now. If anything inside is new or changed on the device, or a folder inside was never opened, the whole folder stays and Finder puts it back. Delete it again to remove it. A folder nested more than 64 levels deep, or holding more than 100,000 items, also stays. A folder that holds a file whose name the Mac can't show stays too; delete it on the device." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A folder on the device named like an app or a document package, such as Tool.app or Notes.rtfd, shows in Finder as an app or a document, because macOS goes by the name. It is read-only on the Mac, with everything in it: edit it on the device, or copy it to the Mac. Something put inside one stays on the Mac, and Finder shows an error for it. Saving one from a Mac app can leave a copy beside it, such as Notes 2.rtfd, which Finder marks with an error, with the edit only on the Mac: copy it to the Mac to keep it. A folder can't be renamed to such a name. To remove one, delete it on the device, or delete the folder that holds it; Finder may put that folder back once, so delete it again." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A package, such as an .rtfd document or an app, can't be copied to the device: compress it into a .zip first. Symbolic links and aliases can't be copied to the device either; Finder shows an error for them." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "A package, such as an .rtfd or Keynote document, an app, a plug-in or a framework, is one item on the Mac but a folder on the device, so Ferry does not copy it. Control-click it, choose **Compress**, and copy the .zip instead." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Add" : {

    },
    "Address" : {

    },
    "After that, on the tester: **Settings** → **System** → **About tester**. Tap **Build number** until developer mode is on." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
